# ================================================================
# silk.cyr -- RFC 6716 SILK decoder (v2.6.1, in progress)
# ================================================================
# The low-bitrate/voice half of Opus. Fixed-point in libopus, so this is an exact
# integer port (int16/int32 widths, arithmetic shifts, saturation emulated in i64).
# Shares the verified ec_dec range coder + `sar`/`_i16` helpers from src/opus.cyr.
#
# Target configs: 1 (SILK NB, 8kHz internal, 20ms) and 9 (SILK WB, 16kHz, 20ms),
# mono, one SILK frame/packet, 4 subframes. Built stage-by-stage, each bit-exact
# vs libopus (silkref/opusdec reference). This file currently covers the LP-layer
# header + silk_decode_indices Steps A-C (signal type, gains, gains dequant, NLSF
# stage-1 index). NLSF stage-2/LPC, pitch/LTP, excitation, synthesis, resample
# are the following bites.

# ---- small iCDF / codebook tables (verbatim from libopus) ----
